  "prefLabel": "Rev 311.02 Form BT-EXT, “Payment Form and Application for 7-Month Extension of Time to File Business Tax Return”",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 311.02 Form BT-EXT, “Payment Form and Application for 7-Month Extension of Time to File Business Tax Return”.\n\n(a) Business organizations that have not paid 100% of their tax liability and need an extension to file their business profits tax return shall:\n\n(1) Pay the remainder of their tax liability; and\n\n(2) Complete and file Form BT-EXT by mail, electronically under Rev 2900, or via the Granite Tax Connect web portal, in accordance with RSA 77-A:9.\n\n(b) Business organizations that have paid 100% of their tax liability and need an extension to file their business profits tax return, shall receive an automatic 7-month extension to file their tax returns without completing Form BT-EXT.\n\n(c) A granted extension of time shall extend the due date of the return, but shall not extend the due date of any payment.\n\nSource. #5490, eff 10-19-92; ss by #6853, eff 9-23-98; ss by #8709, eff 8-25-06 (formerly Rev 311.10); ss by #10758, eff 1-16-15; ss by #14231, eff 4-3-25, EXPIRES 4-3-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev300.html"
